title: other changes
pid: 9dafeaf6-b91c-4707-abe1-e5643f3079fc
body: |2-
  What a node's files changed that no other leaf records ("Other changes
  to a node's file") is one change viewnode under it, its other changes,
  written '(otherChanges KIND...)', a KIND for each way it changed
  ('OtherChange::wire_name'). Its herald says each in the user's words,
  joined by "; ": "its content was reordered; its attribution changed".
  For each list it reordered, its body holds a header naming the list
  and the line diff of the order of the members both graphs give it, as
  a body diff writes one ('-' at HEAD, '+' now, ' ' both): one member a
  line, by its title (an alias by its text, an ID or flag by itself).
  The members drawn under the node stand in the new order, so the body
  holds what the view does not show, the old one. It is one leaf.
